From: bitbonsai <44185+bitbonsai@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep native shell recovery anchoring ready before window show

Optional shell-only MA-007.c recovery-anchor candidate. Native cases UNRUN.
Apply after the currently installed optional stack on Chromium
3e117efa80cec1c4e1e6fbfdf44edeb087a279a5, including complete replacement
0012 SHA-256 8f8023789fdb66841128879766afdb89866c7e393453185336eba69745f66e53
and current 0013/0014/0015. Preserve independent layout rounding.
This delta does not replace 0012 or change the canonical foundation payload.

Sidebar layout hides the app-menu button before startup requests recovery.
The tracked fallback is unavailable until its browser widget becomes visible.
Use a noninteractive BrowserView child at the existing fallback coordinates
only when the opt-in shell reparents the toolbar. A Views anchor is available
before window show and remains drawn when the sidebar is hidden. Keep stock
anchor checks, upstream recovery prompt/actions and browser services intact.

See browser/experiments/native-recovery-anchor.md in myarc for build proof,
regression scope and parent-owned native acceptance still required.

